[Term]
id: DOID:0070805
name: Muggenthaler-Chowdhury-Chioza syndrome
def: "A syndrome characterized by craniofacial dysmorphism, most consistently hypertelorism and a broad flat nose, myopia, and variable additional features including congenital cardiac anomalies, orofacial clefting, and hearing loss that has_material_basis_in homozygous or compound heterozygous mutation in the HYAL2 gene on chromosome 3p21." [url:https\://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/28081210/, url:https\://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34906488/]
