[Term]
id: DOID:0081012
name: critical COVID-19
def: "A COVID-19 that is characterized by the criteria for acute respiratory distress syndrome (ARDS), sepsis, septic shock, or other conditions that would normally require the provision of life sustaining therapies such as mechanical ventilation (invasive or non-invasive) or vasopressor therapy." [url:https\://www.who.int/publications/i/item/WHO-2019-nCoV-clinical-2021-1]
