[Term]
id: DOID:0081309
name: grade II lymphomatoid granulomatosis
def: "A lymphomatoid granulomatosis that is characterized by the presence of occasional large lymphoid cells or immunoblasts in a polymorphous background. Necrosis is more commonly seen as compared to grade I lymphomatoid granulomatosis. By in situ hybridization, EBV-positive cells are readily seen." [url:https\://rarediseases.org/rare-diseases/lymphomatoid-granulomatosis/?filter=ovr-ds-resources]
