id: DOID:0110562
name: autosomal dominant nonsyndromic deafness 33
def: "An autosomal dominant nonsyndromic deafness that has_material_basis_in variation in the chromosome region 13q34." [url:https\://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/19183916/, url:https\://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/37671045/]
comment: Variation in ATP11A, which resides in the chromosome region linked to this disease, 13q34, has been shown to cause autosomal dominant nonsyndromic deafness but evidence does not support it as the cause of this subtype. Reassessment of the haplotype for this disease has suggested that the locus may be inaccurate [JAB].
