def: "A viral infectious disease that results in inflammation located in brain, has_material_basis_in West Nile virus (Orthoflavivirus nilense), which is transmitted_by Culex, Aedes, or Anopheles species of mosquitoes. The infection has_symptom high fever, has_symptom headache, has_symptom neck stiffness, has_symptom stupor, has_symptom disorientation, has_symptom coma, has_symptom tremors, has_symptom convulsions, has_symptom muscle weakness, has_symptom vision loss, has_symptom numbness, and has_symptom paralysis." [url:https\://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC1125772/, url:https\://www.cdc.gov/west-nile-virus/hcp/clinical-signs/]
subset: DO_infectious_disease_slim
subset: DO_rare_slim
subset: zoonotic_infectious_disease
synonym: "West Nile fever encephalitis" EXACT []
synonym: "West Nile Fever with encephalitis" EXACT []
